# The cockpit's noise, for the crew alerts' tones' automatic volume (Sounds/v22-sound.xml's alert entries). Written by
# fdm/cockpitnoise.py from Sounds/v22-sound.xml: do not edit. level(): the A-weighted level of the bank sounds the cockpit
# plays now, dB re full scale at volume 1 (a full-scale sample is FS_SPL dB re 20 uPa), 323 loops of 323 files

var FS_SPL = 134.05;
var TONE_OVER_DB = 20;       # an aural alert's onset over the noise (AC 25.1322-1 appendix 2, 2.d(2)(b): 20 to 30 dB)
var AMBIENT_DB = -71.70;      # the noise taken no lower: a talker's normal vocal effort, re full scale (ANSI S3.5-1997: 62.35 dB SPL)
var AIR_OUT_DB = -3.34;        # FlightGear's output of the bank sounds against level(), all sliders at 1 (measured)
var TONE_OUT_DB = -11.33;      # a tone's onset at gain 1 in the output (the caution chime measured, -10.00; each tone brought to -8.11)

